  "section_notes": "The final rules are strict on reporting (S1) and recall (S5), with mandatory recall at 8/100k and prompt customer notices. S2 requires 55 °C testing and a 5% threshold but only corrective action, not a sales ban, and gives numeric results to customers while shielding them from public release. S3 requires new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months."
